1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,880
Which cities come to mind when you think of international dispute settlement?
提到国际争端解决，你会想到哪些城市？

2
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:41,200
The Hague, Geneva, Singapore.
海牙、日内瓦、新加坡。

3
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:46,519
Well from now on you can add one more to the list, Hong Kong.
从现在起，你可以在名单上再添一个——香港。

4
00:00:46,519 --> 00:00:52,200
The International Organization for Mediation or IOMED was officially inaugurated in the
国际调解组织（IOMED）于2025年10月在香港成立，

5
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:59,960
city in October 2025 as the world's first intergovernmental legal organization dedicated
作为世界上首个致力于通过调解

6
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:04,239
to resolving international disputes through mediation.
解决国际争端的政府间法律组织。

7
00:01:04,239 --> 00:01:11,400
Its mission to fill a gap in a domain traditionally dominated by Western rules and practices.
其使命是填补传统上由西方规则主导的领域的空白。

8
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,799
And things have been moving fast.
而一切进展迅速。

9
00:01:13,799 --> 00:01:20,159
Three years since the idea was first put forward by 19 countries including China, the IOMED
自包括中国在内的19个国家首次提出这一构想三年来，

10
00:01:20,159 --> 00:01:22,159
is now up and running.
IOMED现已成立并运作。

11
00:01:22,159 --> 00:01:23,680
Why the sense of urgency?
为何如此紧迫？

12
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:29,159
How will IOMED mediate differently and will it live up to expectations?
IOMED的调解方式有何不同？能否不负众望？

13
00:01:29,359 --> 00:01:32,280
Welcome to a special edition of The Point with me, Liu Xin.
欢迎收看《对话》特别节目，我是刘欣。

14
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:40,159
I had the pleasure to sit down in Beijing with Teresa Cheng, the first Secretary General of the IOMED.
我在北京与IOMED首任秘书长郑若骅女士进行了对谈。

15
00:01:48,159 --> 00:01:50,359
Professor Cheng, welcome to The Point.
郑教授，欢迎来到《对话》。

16
00:01:50,359 --> 00:01:51,859
Thank you.
谢谢。

17
00:01:51,359 --> 00:01:52,859
Thank you for inviting me.
感谢你的邀请。

18
00:01:52,359 --> 00:01:53,859
It's a great pleasure.
非常荣幸。

19
00:01:53,359 --> 00:01:56,699
Let's find out about this very interesting new institution.
让我们来了解一下这个非常有趣的新机构。

20
00:01:56,740 --> 00:02:01,460
It was initiated by 19 countries including China in 2022.
它由包括中国在内的19个国家于2022年发起。

21
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:07,620
Then in May this year, 33 countries signed up on the convention to establish the IOMED
今年5月，33个国家签署了公约，

22
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:10,539
in Hong Kong, becoming its founding members.
在香港成立IOMED，成为创始成员国。

23
00:02:10,539 --> 00:02:14,140
And in August this year, the convention came into effect.
今年8月，公约生效。

24
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:18,580
And in October this year, the organization was officially inaugurated.
今年10月，该组织正式成立。

25
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:24,900
And by now, correct me if I'm wrong, 37 countries have signed up to the convention and eight
如果我没说错的话，已有37个国家签署了公约，

26
00:02:25,099 --> 00:02:28,099
have ratified it, becoming contracting states.
8个国家已批准，成为缔约国。

27
00:02:28,099 --> 00:02:29,599
Am I accurate?
我说的对吗？

28
00:02:29,099 --> 00:02:36,500
Well, very, except one point is that we now actually have 38 countries that have signed up.
很准确，有一点要纠正，我们现在有38个国家签署了。

29
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:42,460
So as we speak, we have one more from the last time you looked at it and we're expecting more signatory states to join.
就在我们说话这会儿，比你上次了解时又多了一个，我们期待更多签署国加入。

30
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:46,540
So yes, we are a very new body.
所以是的，我们是一个非常新的机构。

31
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:50,980
We've just come into operation for just over a month.
我们刚运作了一个多月。

32
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:56,060
And yet we are a very important, we would think, an international body.
但我们认为，我们是一个非常重要的国际机构。

33
00:02:56,060 --> 00:02:57,560
Congratulations.
祝贺。

34
00:02:57,060 --> 00:03:00,019
I mean, the speed is unprecedented.
这个速度是前所未有的。

